title: Relapsed or refractory nodal TFH lymphoma
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Preferred:'' Clinical trial. Rebiopsy suspected relapse and reassess transplant eligibility early.
* ''Transplant candidates:'' Use salvage therapy to bridge to [[allogeneic transplantation|Allogeneic stem cell transplantation in nodal TFH lymphoma]]. Options include ICE, GDP, DHAP, or GemOx; single agents can also provide disease control.
* ''Targeted/epigenetic options:'' Romidepsin, belinostat, duvelisib, or brentuximab vedotin for CD30-positive disease. Azacitidine is particularly relevant to TFH biology; duvelisib–romidepsin is another option. Several uses are off-label.
* ''Other options:'' Bendamustine, gemcitabine, or lenalidomide; pralatrexate has limited activity in angioimmunoblastic lymphoma.
* ''Without transplantation:'' Select sequential therapies by prior response, toxicity, and patient goals; localized radiotherapy and supportive care can palliate symptoms.

Sources: NCCN T-Cell Lymphomas v2.2026, PTCL-B 4, 6; [[ESMO–EHA 2025|https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12059256/]].
